Actions 1 to 8 are followed by no bytes, 9 to 21 by one, and 22 and up by
two, whether or not the action uses them.

Each sequence consists of sequences of conditions and then actions
each individual condition or action is followed by its parameters. A single
0x7F marks the end of the tables

The automatics table has no verb/noun header. The actions table precedes
each table with two bytes. The first is the verb the second the noun.
A code of 0x7E indicates "any word".

Verbs
0	NONE (noise AND/OR)
1=10	Exits (North, South, East, West, Up, Down,
		NorthEast, NorthWest, SouthEast, SouthWest)

The word table is a single table. It contains 5 bytes per word being 4
letters (space padded, upper case) and a byte of value. Several words may
share a value. It ends XXXX[FF]. The interpreter reads up to five words
of a command. The top bit of the value is set for nouns and clear for
verbs (notes).


Questprobe 3

Flags: the first four slots are the location, the location of the other
character, the carried location and the other character's carried
location. Flag numbers in the engine tables are counted from the slot
after those, so flag n of the game is slot n + 4. Slot 43 is the dark
flag. There are 49 objects and nothing can be worn.

Locations
0xFC	destroyed
0xFD	carried by the Human Torch
0xFE	carried by the Thing

Text: bytes below 0x7B are characters, bytes from 0x7B up are token
numbers (minus 0x7B). A string ends in 0x1F and a table in 0x18. Every
object is a "low" object.

