The room pictures are not drawn by the interpreter on its own: the
automatics table draws them with IMAGE actions.


Section Locations

The file offsets of the tables of every supported release are in
gameinfo.c. The dictionary, token table and some others are located by
searching for known bytes, so that different dumps of the same game work.

A 48K snapshot holds the memory from 4000 up, so in the registry a table
at memory address A of a Spectrum game is at A - 4000.

Memory addresses for Blizzard Pass:

Room Text	75CE	(short descriptions, of the graphical game)
Messages	7E26
Object Text	8CE6
Automatics	96D9
Commands	9A54
Words		A720
Room Exits	AB67
Tokens		B1BC
Object Starts	B6A8
Pictures	B798	(picture scripts, one per room, FF terminated)
Room Text	C000 in RAM bank 6 (long descriptions, of the text game)

Note that blizzard pass is special in that it is the only game for the
Spectrum 128. The 128K version has two location tables (one for what would
be the graphical game and one for the text "other side of the tape" both
placed in one setup, with the rooms in the higher banks). The interpreter
always prints the long descriptions of the text game, which exist for
rooms 0 to 101.
